// shadow_bot.zp — One brain, two bodies
// Multimodal Template — Level 2
//
// Build a chase AI. It works on screen AND on a robot.
// Change ONE line to switch targets.
//
// Codex Labs LLC — 2026

// ── WHICH BODY? ──────────────────────────────
// Uncomment ONE of these two blocks.

// SCREEN MODE (game):
target   : sprite("player")
hunter   : sprite("enemy")
eyes     : sense(target, from: hunter)
legs     : act(hunter.velocity)

// ROBOT MODE (hardware):
// target   : sense(ir_beacon, pin: 2)        // IR beacon on target
// hunter   : self                             // we ARE the robot
// eyes     : sense(distance, pin: 3)          // ultrasonic
// legs     : act(dc_motor, pins: {5, 6})      // two wheels

// ── THE BRAIN (same for both) ────────────────

// How far away is the target?
eyes -> distance_reading

// Decide what to do
distance_reading -> {
    gate(< 50)   -> too_close,
    gate(< 200)  -> chase,
    gate(>= 200) -> search
}

// ── BEHAVIORS ────────────────────────────────

// Too close — back up
too_close -> {
    legs.set(speed: -30),
    wait(500ms)
}

// In range — chase!
chase -> {
    angle_to(target) -> turn_amount,
    turn_amount -> legs.steer(speed: 60)
}

// Lost them — spin to scan
search -> {
    legs.set(left: 40, right: -40)      // spin in place
}

// ── LOOP ─────────────────────────────────────

// Continuous: sense → decide → act
// The chain resolves on every tick.
// Game tick = frame. Robot tick = control loop.

// ── TELEMETRY ────────────────────────────────

distance_reading ~> dashboard("distance")
hunter.state     ~> dashboard("behavior")
eyes             ~> rate(per: 1s) ~> readings_per_second


// ── THE LESSON ───────────────────────────────
//
// The brain doesn't know if it's driving pixels or motors.
// It just reads distance and sends speed.
//
// This is why signal chains matter:
// the logic is separated from the body.
//
// ── TRY THIS ─────────────────────────────────
//
// 1. Change the chase speed. What happens at 100? At 10?
// 2. Change the "too close" distance. Make it cautious (100)
//    or aggressive (20).
// 3. Add a new behavior: "patrol" — move in a square when
//    no target is found. Hint: use a counter and turns.
// 4. Add a second hunter. Do they cooperate or collide?
// 5. Switch from screen to robot. Did you have to change
//    the brain? (No. That's the point.)
